Technical Specification Document: Spaceware – Proxima Descent (Rezona Memeplays Edition)

Version 1 – Core Experience

1. Introduction

This document defines the technical specifications and strategic constraints for adapting the web game "Spaceware: Proxima Descent" to the Rezona (Memeplays) platform.

Primary Objective: Port the core descent-and-survival loop while amplifying the horror theme within Rezona's casual, meme-oriented ecosystem.

Secondary Objective: Establish a reusable specification pattern for horror-educational games inside Rezona, aligning with professional documentation standards (Microsoft, NVIDIA).

Target Platform: Rezona AI Game Generator (web + mobile)

Target Audience: Casual gamers, meme enthusiasts, space horror fans (14–25)

2. Rezona Platform Analysis (Constrained)

Rezona is not a traditional game engine. It is an AI-powered generator optimized for:

· Memeplays: Short (15–90 seconds), replayable, remixable mini-games
· Zero-code creation: Users describe the game in natural language; AI generates logic + assets
· Viral loops: Built-in sharing, remixing, emoji reactions, comments
· Real-time multiplayer (recent addition) – can be used for shared horror experiences

Known Constraints (based on public documentation and community testing):

Area Constraint
Assets No custom uploads (images, models, sounds). Everything is AI-generated on the fly.
Graphics No shaders, no post-processing, no particle systems. SVG/vector-based only.
Physics No rigidbody, no collision detection beyond simple bounding boxes.
Animation No frame-by-frame. SVG transforms (translate, rotate, scale) only.
Audio Basic bleeps and sweeps. No ambient layers or dynamic mixing.
Logic Procedural generation is limited. Most logic is event-driven (if-then).
Performance 60 fps target, but heavy SVG scenes drop frames. Keep objects under 50.

Opportunities (not limitations):

· High remixability: Your game can be forked and modded by the community. Horror can spread.
· Fast iteration: AI generates a playable version in seconds. Test → adjust → reprompt.
· Social horror: Shared anxiety works well with Rezona's emoji/comment system.
· Rezonasaur as a narrative element: The mascot can appear as a jumpscare or environmental detail.

3. Porting Strategy: Horror Within Casual Constraints

Instead of fighting the platform, we translate horror mechanics into what Rezona does best.

Traditional Horror Element Rezona Adaptation
High-fidelity gore / blood SVG wireframe damage (white lines turning red, cracks on ship)
Dynamic lighting / shadows High contrast: black background, white/red elements only
Complex AI enemy behavior Scripted patterns + random flicker of HUD elements
Atmospheric sound Simple bleeps + silence (silence is scarier than bad audio)
Jump scares Sudden appearance of Rezonasaur or a close asteroid
Psychological tension Decreasing oxygen bar + unpredictable asteroid waves

4. Core Game Loop (Version 1)

The game is an inverse infinite runner with a horror-educational twist.

Setup:

· Player controls the Janax-M1 spacecraft.
· Starting altitude: 40,000
· Goal: Reach altitude 0 (land on Proxima Centauri B)
· Obstacles: Asteroids generated as SVG polygons

Controls:

· Left / Right (or tap left/right on mobile) → move ship horizontally
· No braking (descent speed is constant)

Mechanics:

· Each asteroid collision reduces altitude by 500 (penalty) AND reduces integrity bar (visual feedback)
· Integrity bar: starts at 100%. At 0%, the ship explodes → game over
· No lives. One mistake chain can kill you.
· Oxygen bar (decreases over time, not shown in V1 but reserved for V2)

Victory Condition:

· Altitude reaches 0 → Phase 1 completed
· Landing cutscene (SVG animation of ship touching down)

Defeat Condition:

· Integrity reaches 0 → explosion animation + "MISSION FAILED" + restart button

5. Horror Amplification Mechanics (V1)

Within Rezona's constraints, we add three lightweight horror elements:

5.1 HUD Flicker

· When integrity drops below 30%, the HUD (altitude, integrity bars) flickers randomly (opacity 50% ↔ 100% every 0.2–0.5s).
· Creates anxiety. No code complexity.

5.2 Unpredictable Asteroid Waves

· Not random. Patterned but with occasional "bursts": 5 asteroids in 2 seconds.
· The player cannot fully predict. Paranoia.

5.3 The Rezonasaur Jumpscare (Rare)

· 1% chance per asteroid wave.
· Instead of an asteroid, the Rezonasaur face appears briefly (white wireframe outline) and disappears.
· No damage. Just a "what was that?" moment.
· Meme-friendly. Community will remix it.

6. Asset Specification (AI-Generated)

Do not upload anything. Describe.

6.1 Ship (Janax-M1)

· Style: Low-poly SVG, white wireframe on black background
· Shape: Triangle with two side wings, no fill, stroke width 2
· Size: 5% of screen width
· Position: Bottom third, centered

6.2 Asteroids

· Style: Irregular polygons, white stroke, no fill
· Size: Random between 2% and 6% of screen width
· Behavior: Move from top to bottom, horizontal drift ±20% of width per asteroid

6.3 Background

· Style: Black void, no stars (stars added in V2)
· Purpose: High contrast for white/red elements. Silence as horror.

6.4 Integrity Bar

· Style: White outline bar, red fill
· Position: Top right
· Width: 30% of screen

6.5 Altitude Counter

· Font: Monospace, white, large
· Position: Top center
· Format: "ALT: 40,000"

7. Horror Pacing Guide (For AI Prompts)

Altitude Range Feeling Mechanics
40,000 – 30,000 Calm, tutorial Slow asteroids, no flicker. Player learns controls.
29,999 – 15,000 Tension building Moderate asteroid speed, occasional bursts. Oxygen not shown yet.
14,999 – 5,000 Anxiety HUD flicker at integrity <30%. Waves become unpredictable.
4,999 – 1 Panic Rezonasaur jumpscare possible. Asteroids fast. Player fights to survive.
0 Relief / Horror of the unknown Landing cutscene. Silence. Player knows something is waiting.

8. Integration with Future Versions (V2, V3)

V1 ends at landing. V2 will add:

· Surface exploration (tycoon mechanics)
· Oxygen management
· Flashcards (educational)
· Leviathan cosmic horror (rare events)

V1 must not break when V2 code is added. Use a gamePhase variable:

· "DESCENT" (V1)
· "LANDING" (cutscene)
· "SURVIVAL" (V2, not implemented yet, but reserved)

9. Success Metrics for V1

Metric Target
Playable from start to landing 100% (no crashes)
Average playtime 2–4 minutes (good for memeplay)
Horror perception User test: "did you feel tension?" → >70% yes
Replayability Player tries at least 3 times
Remix rate At least 1 community remix within 2 weeks

10. Deliverable

A fully functional Rezona game (single HTML/JS block) that implements:

· Descent from 40,000 to 0 with asteroid dodging
· Integrity bar and altitude counter
· HUD flicker at low integrity
· Unpredictable asteroid waves
· Rare Rezonasaur jumpscare
· Victory landing cutscene (SVG animation)
· Defeat explosion + restart

All assets generated by AI from textual descriptions. No external files.

